many times I prepared myself, went over the things I intended to say, to ask. I always came off sounding like a weak, stuttering fool.
\par \tab He- I would continue to assume that, seeing as how he\rquote d explicitly said he wasn\rquote t a woman and there was no other option that made sense- didn\rquote t turn, his slim figure silhouetted against the firelight. He was wearing a tailored 
vest that was somehow still loose around the hips, and a dark shirt beneath that was certainly too big and billowed at the arms. Unlike him\'85 he\rquote d always been dressed tailored and fitted. These must have been second-hand clothes. 
Britches, dark as well, hugged his figure yet still, somehow, gave nothing about his anatomy away.
