\par \tab He was scared. I got a whiff of the fear, subtle but distinct. He didn\rquote t trust his bindings, I realized. I tugged again.
\par \tab No chance. I was too weak, and however he\rquote d bound me, it tightened the more I pulled.
\par \tab He stood beside me now, about a foot away, smiling wanly. Teacup held at the ready. But he also had a blade on his person, at the hip. I didn\rquote t miss it.
\par \tab \'93You were heavy,\'94 he said, with a light huff of a laugh. It was a genuine laugh, like in the courtyard. I\rquote d heard it many times since, in my dreams. Hearing it again, in person, was almost too much. \'93No offense meant, I just\'85
